            <ArticleTitle>Killer ILCs in the Fat.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>169-171</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1074-7613(17)30039-0</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.immuni.2017.02.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Innate lymphoid cells (ILCs) residing in adipose tissue participate in the pathogenesis of obesity, but their contribution toward adipose tissue homeostasis in the lean state is unclear. Boulenouar et al. (2017) now report that heterogenous type 1 ILCs in adipose tissues regulate macrophage homeostasis through cytotoxicity.</AbstractText>
